---
description: Thin Angular components — signals, no template logic sprawl
globs: web/**/*.{ts,html}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Angular components

- Standalone + `OnPush`. Prefer `inject()`, `input()` / `output()`, signals.
- Do not call methods from templates for derived UI — use `computed` (or precomputed fields on row models, e.g. `widthClass`).
- Keep `@for` / `@if` in templates; keep sorting, filtering, and class derivation in the class or a pure helper.
- Import models/constants/enums from `models/` and `constants/` — do not redefine them in the component file.
- Services own HTTP, error mapping, and reusable presentation helpers (e.g. `TailwindWidthService`); components subscribe / call and update signals.
- Do not keep ratio→class / formatting tables as free functions in component files — put thresholds in `constants/`, logic in a service.
